[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3730172621","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/114805#issuecomment-3730172621","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114805","id":3730172621,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7eVerN","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-09T18:50:37Z","updated_at":"2026-01-09T18:55:41Z","body":"This is not how input is properly done, and relying on echo events is not how game input should be accomplished, I don't think this is a situation that is problematic in normal usage and expected usage of input events\n\nThe documentation clearly describes how to properly handle input in games\n\nI don't understand what real problem this is reporting, no one is using input for movement this way\n\nFor the order of echo events that would be expected I'd say as you're not pressing them exactly the same time, they'll be repeated with an interval after you pressed them","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3730172621/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3730190648","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/114805#issuecomment-3730190648","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114805","id":3730190648,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7eVjE4","user":{"login":"ghost","id":10137,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMTM3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10137?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost","html_url":"https://github.com/ghost","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-09T18:55:45Z","updated_at":"2026-01-09T18:59:30Z","body":"I think this might be an implementation issue instead of engine. Have you tried for accounting for combinations in the first set of elifs? Im not sure I understand the second elseif.  I think a better way to implement this is:\n\n1. Get which keys are being held down using ```Input.is_key_pressed(keycode)``` out of AWSD.\n\n2. Use object's transform **(local space)** to move in a direction. You can add any two directional vectors of an object's transforms, then normalize them to get a diagonal direction. For example: ```(object.get_global_transform().basis.z + object.get_global_transform().basis.y).normalized()```. This will give a **diagonal direction vector** that goes upwards and forwards.\n\nNOTE : AWSD inputs would pretty much map out to the objects transforms. So A would map to ```object.get_global_transform().basis.x``` and D to ```-object.get_global_transform().basis.x```.  Just a little clarification.\n\nHope this helps! Good luck.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3730190648/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3730233873","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/114805#issuecomment-3730233873","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114805","id":3730233873,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7eVtoR","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-09T19:09:14Z","updated_at":"2026-01-09T19:09:14Z","body":"The issue report is about the behavior itself, not their movement code not working, so this suggestion isn't very relevant IMO, instead we should focus on if there is a bug here or not, not how to write more useful control code","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3730233873/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3730446315","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/114805#issuecomment-3730446315","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114805","id":3730446315,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7eWhfr","user":{"login":"AviseOffical","id":113899383,"node_id":"U_kgDOBsn3dw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/113899383?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AviseOffical","html_url":"https://github.com/AviseOffical","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AviseOffical/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AviseOffical/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AviseOffical/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AviseOffical/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AviseOffical/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AviseOffical/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AviseOffical/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AviseOffical/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AviseOffical/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-09T20:19:04Z","updated_at":"2026-01-09T20:28:35Z","body":"u can use Godot's CharacterBody3D template script and u can see it. make the ground have a texture with grid like prototype textures and if u look at the floor while going diagonal \"w+d\" and u stop pressing the keys u will see that u move forward then slide right.\n\n\n[Edit]\nso the default CharacterBody3D template script does velocity.x = direction.x * speed with does not have a problem but when using acceleration and friction.\n\nthis code u can see it:\n```\nextends CharacterBody3D\n\nconst SPEED = 5.0\nconst ACCEL = 10.0      # How fast you reach max speed\nconst FRICTION = 15.0   # How fast you stop on the ground\nconst AIR_RESISTANCE = 2.0 # How much control you have in the air\nconst JUMP_VELOCITY = 4.5\nconst MOUSE_SENSITIVITY = 0.003\n\n@onready var head: Node3D = $Head\n\nfunc _ready() -> void:\n\tInput.set_mouse_mode(Input.MOUSE_MODE_CAPTURED)\n\nfunc _unhandled_input(event: InputEvent) -> void:\n\tif event is InputEventMouseMotion:\n\t\trotate_y(-event.relative.x * MOUSE_SENSITIVITY)\n\t\thead.rotate_x(-event.relative.y * MOUSE_SENSITIVITY)\n\t\thead.rotation.x = clamp(head.rotation.x, deg_to_rad(-89), deg_to_rad(89))\n\n\tif event.is_action_pressed(\"ui_cancel\"):\n\t\tif Input.get_mouse_mode() == Input.MOUSE_MODE_CAPTURED:\n\t\t\tInput.set_mouse_mode(Input.MOUSE_MODE_VISIBLE)\n\t\telse:\n\t\t\tInput.set_mouse_mode(Input.MOUSE_MODE_CAPTURED)\n\nfunc _physics_process(delta: float) -> void:\n\t# Add the gravity.\n\tif not is_on_floor():\n\t\tvelocity += get_gravity() * delta\n\n\t# Handle jump.\n\tif Input.is_action_just_pressed(\"ui_accept\") and is_on_floor():\n\t\tvelocity.y = JUMP_VELOCITY\n\n\t# Get input direction\n\tvar input_dir := Input.get_vector(\"strafe_left\", \"strafe_right\", \"move_forward\", \"move_backward\")\n\tvar direction := (transform.basis * Vector3(input_dir.x, 0, input_dir.y)).normalized()\n\t\n\t# Determine which logic to use: Acceleration or Friction\n\tvar target_vel = direction * SPEED\n\tvar accel_rate = 0.0\n\t\n\tif direction:\n\t\t# We are moving\n\t\taccel_rate = ACCEL if is_on_floor() else AIR_RESISTANCE\n\telse:\n\t\t# We are sliding to a stop\n\t\taccel_rate = FRICTION if is_on_floor() else AIR_RESISTANCE\n\n\t# Apply the movement\n\tvelocity.x = move_toward(velocity.x, target_vel.x, accel_rate * delta)\n\tvelocity.z = move_toward(velocity.z, target_vel.z, accel_rate * delta)\n\n\tmove_and_slide()\n```","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3730446315/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3732542172","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/114805#issuecomment-3732542172","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114805","id":3732542172,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7eehLc","user":{"login":"AviseOffical","id":113899383,"node_id":"U_kgDOBsn3dw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/113899383?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AviseOffical","html_url":"https://github.com/AviseOffical","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AviseOffical/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AviseOffical/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AviseOffical/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AviseOffical/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AviseOffical/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AviseOffical/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AviseOffical/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AviseOffical/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AviseOffical/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-10T12:18:25Z","updated_at":"2026-01-10T12:18:25Z","body":"I did some more testing and it seems to be the move_toward function that is the root cause.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3732542172/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3732741491","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/114805#issuecomment-3732741491","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114805","id":3732741491,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7efR1z","user":{"login":"AviseOffical","id":113899383,"node_id":"U_kgDOBsn3dw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/113899383?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AviseOffical","html_url":"https://github.com/AviseOffical","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AviseOffical/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AviseOffical/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AviseOffical/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AviseOffical/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AviseOffical/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AviseOffical/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AviseOffical/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AviseOffical/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AviseOffical/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-10T13:19:15Z","updated_at":"2026-01-10T13:19:15Z","body":"does anyone know how to do diagonal movement where it allows me to set acceleration and friction without using move_toward?","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.c